From 8f72706118a087438fb09e6b28b097ee1af391bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:07:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] G2-EX step 1: clipped redraw in the retained stage
 (exact), idle lane parts without boxes

A layer that did not change but lies on a dirty box used to be put back and drawn over its whole box,
which dragged every layer on that box into the redraw (the demon's bob redrew the whole host frame, a
dialogue box redrew Fuzz, the candles, the curtains and the host...). The stage now draws such a layer
(stage_layer_clip: only plat_rect, plat_shade_rect and plat_image at scale 1) through the pieces of the
dirty set that lie in its box, clipped to each (stage_clip_n / stage_clip_get, plat_clip); the dirty set
no longer grows through them. The dirty set is cut once into disjoint pieces (build_pieces, adjacent
equal spans joined) instead of twice by restore_dirty.
GBA: gba_nodraw mode 7 (GBA_NODRAW_CLIP); plat_rect jumps to stage_clip_rect (ARM, room group, +16 B of
resident IWRAM in plat_rect), plat_shade_rect and plat_image cut themselves (images by cropped rows).
Native: plat_clip honoured by rects, shades, images, and a counter for the calls it cannot honour.
Exorcism: the host frame (scale 1 with a picture), candles, Fuzz, the demon (scale 1), the faith meter
and the church parts are clippable layers; the lane's feedback pop and count-in parts have an empty box
while they draw nothing.
Tests: test_stage_clip.c (the primitives under a clip against the unclipped call; the stage keeps a
clipped layer from widening the dirty set; pieces disjoint and covering), test_stage.c (the ritual,
stage on / off, uses the clip on >= 1/4 of its frames and makes no call a clip does not honour).
GBA full-ritual frames (1,252, deterministic portraits) identical to the base ROM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
